  "details": "1. Create a new Toon Standard material and inspect it.\n\n2. Enable Detail texture, Specular, Matcap and/or Rim Lighting in a Toon Standard material by clicking on the checkbox. (E.g., Rim Lighting is enabled and set to a red color.)\n\n3. Right click the new Toon Shader material, Create → Material Variant, and inspect it.\n\n4. Notice the checkboxes for Detail texture, Specular, Matcap and Rim Lighting revert back to disabled state, but retain their other settings.\n\nVideo: https://files.catbox.moe/yn99hs.mp4\n\nGenerally, Material Variants remember their checkbox states between different shaders (i.e. Unity Standard, lilToon, Poiyomi). Mobile Toon Standard doesn't (yet).\n\nUnity 2022.3.22f1\n\nSDK 3.8.1-beta.3",
